message: >
  If you use this software in a publication, please cite it using the
  metadata below.  To mint a permanent DOI, enable the repository on
  Zenodo and create a GitHub release — see the README for the full
  procedure.
title: "jwspecfit: resolution-aware emission-line fitting, MCMC sampling, and chemical abundances for JWST NIRSpec"
abstract: >
  jwspecfit is a coordinated suite of three Python packages for the
  analysis of JWST NIRSpec spectra: least-squares Gaussian line fitting
  with resolution-aware bin-averaged profiles (jwspecfit), Bayesian MCMC
  fitting via NUTS, emcee, or nautilus (jwspecmcmc), and chemical
  abundance derivation via direct-Te (PyNEB), Bayesian forward model
  (Cullen+25), or strong-line calibrations (Sanders+25) with
  Balmer-decrement dust correction anchored on Halpha or Hbeta
  (jwspecabund).
type: software
